/**
 * Ledger is Kadé's double-entry book. It is driven almost entirely by events (exactly-once effects via
 * processed_events + one journal entry per source event id) and is the read model for every money
 * screen: restaurant sales and weekly statements, admin payout batches, rider earnings, cash held,
 * settlements, deposits and the refunds ledger. Every journal entry balances (Σ debits = Σ credits).
 *
 * Postings (amounts come from the event snapshots; F = food = subtotal, C = commission =
 * commission_bps × F, Rf = restaurant-funded discounts (saving + restaurant-funded promo),
 * Kp = Kadé-funded promo):
 *   OrderDelivered/Collected  Dr ORDER_CLEARING   total + credit      Cr RESTAURANT_PAYABLE  F − C − Rf
 *                             Dr PROMO_EXPENSE    Kp                  Cr COMMISSION_REVENUE  C
 *                                                                     Cr DELIVERY_FEE_REVENUE delivery_fee
 *                                                                     Cr SERVICE_FEE_REVENUE small_order_fee
 *                                                                     Cr RIDER_PAYABLE       tip
 *   PaymentCaptured (card)    Dr PSP_CLEARING                         Cr ORDER_CLEARING
 *   PaymentCaptured (cash)    Dr RIDER_CASH_HELD                      Cr ORDER_CLEARING   (rider holds Kadé's cash)
 *   CustomerCreditChanged     ORDER_SPEND:          Dr CUSTOMER_CREDIT  Cr ORDER_CLEARING
 *                             ORDER_SPEND_REVERSED: Dr ORDER_CLEARING   Cr CUSTOMER_CREDIT
 *                             GOODWILL/REFERRAL:    Dr PROMO_EXPENSE    Cr CUSTOMER_CREDIT
 *                             GIFT_CARD:            Dr GIFT_CARD_LIABILITY Cr CUSTOMER_CREDIT
 *                             REFUND: not posted here (posted once, from OrderRefunded)
 *   DeliveryCompleted         Dr DELIVERY_COST  base+distance+boost   Cr RIDER_PAYABLE
 *   OrderRefunded             Dr REFUND_EXPENSE, or RESTAURANT_PAYABLE when the restaurant is at fault
 *                                                                     Cr PSP_CLEARING (card) / CUSTOMER_CREDIT (credit)
 *                             (PaymentRefunded only confirms the PSP side; it posts nothing.)
 *   RecordCashDeposit         Dr BANK                                 Cr RIDER_CASH_HELD
 *   SettleRider               Dr RIDER_PAYABLE                        Cr RIDER_CASH_HELD (offset), Cr BANK (rest)
 *   MarkPayoutBatchPaid       Dr RESTAURANT_PAYABLE                   Cr BANK
 * Balance check for a delivered order: total + credit + Kp = F − Rf + delivery_fee + small_order_fee + tip.
 */
